description: Start repo coding tasks in poteto-mode by default (pstack)
alwaysApply: true
---
# pstack default

- Repo coding task (you will edit code in a git repo): start with the `poteto-mode` skill. Model roles come from `pstack-models.mdc`.
- Trivial edit (typo, one-line config, version bump): skip poteto-mode and say so in one line.
- Not a coding task (chat, brainstorm, ops, account or infra admin): do not start poteto-mode.
- Opt out: if the request says "no poteto-mode", "skip pstack", or "quick fix, no pstack", do not start it.
- Opt in anywhere: "@poteto-mode", "/poteto-mode", or "run poteto-mode".
- Company repos (origin not under github.com/benoror, for example a work or client org): do not start poteto-mode unless the request opens it explicitly. Never carry context, files, or notes from a company repo into a personal repo, or the reverse.
